size. Baloo is built over previous lookup arguments, and the framework for SNARKs from Ràfols and Zapico (CRYPTO 21). Our protocol supports commit-and-prove expansions: the prover selects the subtable containing the elements used in the lookup, that is unknown to the verifier, commits to it and later proves its relation with the committed elements.\nL44: This feature makes Baloo especially suitable for proving input-output relations on hash functions, and in particular to instantiate the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM).\nL45: ##### Metadata\nL46: Available format(s)\nL47:     【17†PDF】\nL48: Category\nL49:     【18†Cryptographic protocols】\nL50: Publication info\nL51:     Published by the IACR in CIC 2025\nL52: Keywords\nL53:     【19†SNARK】【20†Lookup】【21†Scalability】【22†EVM】\nL54: Contact author(s)\nL55:     arantxa zapico @ upf edu\nL56: ariel gabizon @ gmail com\nL57: khovratovich @ gmail com\nL58: mary maller @ ethereum org\nL59: carla rafols @ upf edu\nL60: History\nL61:     2025-07-08: revised\nL62:     2022-11-10: received\nL63:     【23†See all versions】\nL64: Short URL\nL65:     【24†https://ia.cr/2022/1565†ia.cr】\nL66: License\nL67: 【25†CC BY†creativecommons.org】\nL68: BibTeX 【26†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL69: \nL70:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2022/1565,\nL71:           author = {Arantxa Zapico and Ariel Gabizon and Dmitry Khovratovich and Mary Maller and Carla Ràfols},\nL72:           title = {Baloo: Nearly Optimal Lookup Arguments},\nL73:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2022/1565},\nL74:           year = {2022},\nL75:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2022/1565}\nL76:     }\nL77: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nfeat(sumcheck,binary-pcs,lookup,multilinear-util)!: enforce caller soundness obligations instead of documenting them by tcoratger · Pull Request #2293 · Plonky3/Plonky3 · GitHub (https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3/pull/2293)\nciteturn6view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view2\",\"pattern\":\"merged commit\"}); Total lines: 661\nL582:     looks inapplicable to a fixture naming 128 bits, which is exactly the fixture\nL583:     it caught. The test now runs 0/0, 0/20, 20/20 and 128/128, so the condition is\nL584:     pinned rather than described.\nL585: \nL586:     The cross-AIR bus check returns the widest global payload, starting from zero.\nL587:     The figure a challenge table is built from takes the max over local lookups too\nL588:     and starts from one, so an AIR with only local lookups gets zero from one and\nL589:     one from the other. Saying \"global\" keeps the two from being conflated while\nL590:     the gap between them is still open.\nL591: \nL592:     The obligations page said the schedule floor covers every route to a config.\nL593:     It covers every constructor: the fields are public and the verifier does not\nL594:     recount.\nL595: \nL596:     Closes 【81†Plonky3#2271】\nL597: \nL598:     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nL599: Hide details View details\nL600: \nL601: 【70†tcoratger】 merged commit 【126†`669fcae`】 into Plonky3:main 【127†Sep 22, 2026】\nL602: \nL603: 23 checks passed\nL604: ### Uh oh!\nL605: \nL606: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL607: \nL608: 【128†gopikannappan】 mentioned this pull request 【129†Sep 23, 2026】\nL609: \nL610: 【130†test(commit): pin every multilinear backend's commit binding against its verifier's #2308】\nL611: \nL612: Merged\nL613: \nL614: 【131†Sign up for free】 to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? 【1†Sign in to comment】\nL615: \nL616: [Input] [Input]\nL617: \nL618: ### Reviewers\nL619: \nL620: 【83†Nashtare】 Nashtare approved these changes\nL621: ### Uh oh!\nL622: \nL623: There was an error while loading. Please re